+* `2` — `DIR` or an output file in it could not be written, or `--out-dir`
+  was given without a named `FILE`. Reported on standard error the same way.
 
 ## What is deliberately left alone
 
@@ -59,6 +92,11 @@ $ PYTHONPATH=src python -m logredact app.log > app.redacted.log
 * Digit runs shorter than 13 or longer than 19 digits, and digits glued to
   letters (`deadbeef4111111111111111`).
 * `user=jane@example.com` keeps its `user=` prefix; only the address goes.
+* Phone numbers not written in international form: `14155552671`,
+  `0014155552671`, `(415) 555-2671`. Only a leading `+` marks a number.
+* `+1234567` (7 digits) and `+1234567890123456` (16 digits) are outside the
+  8-15 digit range, and the longer one is left whole rather than having its
+  first 15 digits redacted.
 
 A card number may be written in groups (`4111 1111 1111 1111`,
 `4111-1111-1111-1111`), but a doubled separator ends the number, so
@@ -74,12 +112,19 @@ src/logredact/__main__.py    python -m logredact
 tests/test_logredact.py      unit and end-to-end tests
